Spec: Owner-approved mutual TLS device identity

Purpose:
  Authenticate device possession of approved P-256 keys through standard TLS and a private owner trust root.

Owns:
  ./SecureIdentity.cs

References:
  /docs/adr/0013-secure-direct-streams.md

Must:
  Validate chain, time, EKU and server name before accepting an explicitly approved peer SPKI fingerprint.
  Generate device keys locally and sign only validated CSRs with fixed non-CA device extensions.
  Keep private keys in protected owner state without modifying system certificate trust or returning keys to applications.
  Use TLS `1.2` or `1.3`; reject unknown, revoked, expired, wrong-root or wrong-pin devices without insecure fallback.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Verify local CSR issuance, actual mutual TLS and owner CLI enrollment without exposing device keys.
